The important part is that the phones don't need cellular internet or a mobile network.

ESP32 creates a Wi-Fi network.
Phone connects to the ESP32's Wi-Fi.
User opens 192.168.4.1 in a browser.
ESP32 serves the chat interface.
A message is sent from Phone 1 → ESP32 #1.
ESP32 #1 sends the message through LoRa.
ESP32 #2 receives it.
ESP32 #2 sends it to Phone 2 through Wi-Fi.
The message appears in the browser-based chat.
